description:
Quick links:  5-Year UV Warranty  |  Installation Guide & Video  |  Eco Plant Cleaner  |  Need seamless coverage? See the 3m Boxwood Roll    Designer Plants’ Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel is Australia’s most specified UV-resistant greenery panel, trusted across more than 55,000 residential and commercial installations by interior designers, landscape architects, and commercial operators. Each panel arrives ready to install — no specialist tools, no landscaping knowledge required. The panel is constructed from low-density polyethylene (LDPE) with RealTex UV inhibitors integrated directly into the leaf material — not applied as a surface coating. This manufacturing method ensures the colour, density, and texture remain consistent across years of direct outdoor exposure without specialist treatment or reapplication.   Specifications    Dimensions 100cm × 100cm (1m × 1m)   Coverage per panel 1m²   Material Low-density polyethylene (LDPE) with integrated RealTex UV inhibitors   UV certification ISO-certified UV resistant — UVTex inhibitors integrated within the leaf, not surface-applied   Indoor / Outdoor Suitable for both indoor and outdoor installation   Frost resistance Yes — frost resistant   Warranty 5 years (UV-certified outdoor installations)   Recyclable Yes — 100% recyclable LDPE. Designer Plants operates Australia’s only artificial greenery recycling programme   Installation methods Screws with washers, zip ties, or staples depending on surface type   Panel joining Panels interlock and can be trimmed to size with standard scissors   Toxic substances Non-toxic — lab tested, safe for use in spaces with children and animals      Where Designer Plants Boxwood Panels Are Used A 1m² panel. Endless possibilities. These are the spaces it most commonly transforms — though the list is far from complete. Fence lines and boundary walls That tired timber paling or bare brick boundary deserves better. Panels clip together and mount directly to existing surfaces in an afternoon — no landscaper, no permanent modification, no waiting for something to grow. Pool surrounds and outdoor entertaining Picture the resort backdrop that makes every weekend feel like a getaway. UV-stabilised at the leaf level, the panels hold their colour through Australian summers and years of direct sun without a second thought. Reception areas and lobby feature walls The wall behind the desk sets the tone for everything that follows. A floor-to-ceiling boxwood installation communicates quality and permanence — without the irrigation system a living wall requires. Restaurants, cafes, and hospitality venues Give every table something worth photographing. Define zones, soften the acoustics, and create the atmosphere that brings people back. FireTex fire-rated variants available for venues with commercial building code requirements. Offices and workplace interiors Greenery changes how a workspace feels — measurably. Boardrooms, breakout zones, and open-plan floors all benefit from the texture and calm that botanical elements bring, with none of the upkeep. Retail, events, and branded activations Installs in hours. Relocates without damage. Photographs as the real thing. From a two-day pop-up to a permanent flagship fit-out — the panel works equally hard in both. Specified for activations by Aperol, BMW, and Disney. Childcare, healthcare, and education SafeTex-certified and non-toxic — built for the environments where material safety is non-negotiable. In active use across childcare centres, schools, medical waiting rooms, and aged care facilities across Australia. Photography and content creation The depth and texture reads as the real thing on camera. A permanent backdrop that earns its footprint every time the shutter opens — no paint, no fabric, nothing that dates.  The panel has also found its way onto gymnasium walls, rooftop terraces, carpark screening, heritage building facades, showroom displays, stairwell features, balcony privacy screens, and temporary festival structures. If a space has a vertical surface, there is a strong chance it belongs there. Call Designer Plants on 1800 617 341 to talk through a specific brief.    Installation Each panel is designed for DIY installation on any flat vertical surface. Panels are trimmed to size with ordinary scissors and joined using interlocking edges. On brick or masonry surfaces, wall plugs and screws with washers are recommended. On timber fencing, screws or staples applied through the backing grid provide a clean finish. On balcony railings, zip ties allow installation and removal without leaving a mark. A step-by-step installation guide with video walkthrough is available in the Resource Hub. Designer Plants’ installation team is also available for commercial projects and large-scale residential installations across Australia.   Why Designers and Commercial Operators Specify Designer Plants Designer Plants holds a 5-star rating across more than 20,000 verified customer reviews and has delivered commercial-grade installations for clients including BMW, Disney, Aperol, Facebook, Coca-Cola, Westfield, Virgin Australia, and VicRoads. A 5-year UV warranty is provided on all certified outdoor panels. Designer Plants is Australia’s only artificial greenery supplier with a dedicated product recycling programme — an important consideration for sustainability-conscious commercial briefs. Trade pricing and wholesale accounts are available. Contact the team on 1800 617 341 or at sales@designerplants.com.au to discuss project requirements.   Maintenance No watering, pruning, fertilising, or pest control is required. For outdoor panels, an occasional rinse with water removes dust accumulation. Designer Plants’ Eco-Friendly Artificial Plant Cleaner is available for indoor installations where a spotless finish is required year-round.   Frequently Asked Questions    Is the Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel suitable for outdoor use in Australia?  Yes. The panel is ISO-certified UV resistant and engineered for Australian outdoor conditions including direct sun exposure and frost. UV inhibitors are integrated within the leaf material — not applied as a surface coating — ensuring colour retention across years of outdoor exposure without reapplication. A 5-year UV warranty applies to all outdoor installations.    How do I install the Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel?  Each 1m × 1m panel is designed for DIY installation on any flat vertical surface. On masonry surfaces, attach using wall plugs and screws with washers. On timber fencing, screws or staples through the backing grid provide a clean finish. On balcony railings, zip ties allow installation and removal without leaving a mark. Panels trim to any size with standard scissors and interlock seamlessly for continuous coverage. A full step-by-step installation guide with video walkthrough is available in the Resource Hub.    How many panels are needed to cover a wall or fence?  Each panel covers exactly 1m². To calculate the number of panels required, multiply the wall height (in metres) by the width (in metres) and round up to the nearest whole number. Designer Plants provides a coverage calculator on the website for larger or irregular spaces. For commercial projects, the specification team is available on 1800 617 341.    What is the warranty on the Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel?  Designer Plants provides a 5-year UV warranty on outdoor installations of the Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel. The warranty covers colour retention and structural integrity under normal outdoor conditions including direct Australian sun exposure.    Can the panels be used in commercial environments?  Yes. The Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel is specified for commercial use across hospitality venues, retail fit-outs, office interiors, and large-scale feature wall installations. Designer Plants has delivered commercial-grade installations for clients including BMW, Disney, Aperol, Facebook, Coca-Cola, Westfield, Virgin Australia, and VicRoads. Trade pricing and wholesale accounts are available — contact the team on 1800 617 341 to discuss project requirements.    Are the panels safe for use around children and animals?  Yes. The panels are constructed from lab-tested, non-toxic LDPE materials and are SafeTex certified — meaning no harmful substances are released in indoor environments. The panels are in use across family homes, childcare facilities, and pet-friendly commercial spaces.    Are the panels recyclable?  Yes. Each panel is constructed from 100% recyclable low-density polyethylene (LDPE). Designer Plants operates Australia’s only dedicated artificial greenery recycling programme, allowing customers to return panels at end of life rather than sending them to landfill.    What is the difference between the Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel and the Premium Boxwood Roll?  The 1m × 1m Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel is the standard modular option — ideal for most residential and commercial installations where individual panel joins are acceptable. The Premium Boxwood Roll (3m × 1m) eliminates joins across wide surfaces and is preferred for continuous fence lines, event backdrops, and commercial screening projects where a seamless finish is critical.    How much does delivery cost?  Delivery costs vary based on the items ordered and destination. Exact costs are calculated at checkout. As a guide, standard delivery on larger items typically ranges from $15–$40. Designer Plants caps delivery fees to a low flat rate regardless of actual carrier cost. Free delivery applies on qualifying orders — any promotional or repeat-client delivery code must be applied prior to checkout. Orders are typically dispatched same day or next business day.    How many green wall or hedge panels are needed?  The number of panels required is calculated by multiplying the length and width of the wall in metres. For example, a wall measuring 5m wide by 2m high requires 10 panels (each covering 1m²). For irregular shapes or larger commercial projects, Designer Plants provides a dedicated artificial green wall coverage calculator to determine the exact quantity needed.    What are artificial green walls?  Artificial green walls are modular panel systems designed to replicate the appearance of a living green wall without the ongoing maintenance, irrigation, or structural requirements of planted alternatives. Designer Plants’ artificial green walls are constructed using RealTex materials — a proprietary blend engineered to replicate the colour variation, texture, and density of natural foliage with botanical accuracy. Each panel is UV-stabilised for outdoor durability and assembled by hand to ensure no two panels have an identical, uniform appearance. The result is a premium architectural greenery installation suited to residential, commercial, and hospitality environments across Australia.    How much does delivery cost, and how long will my order take to arrive?  Designer Plants offers free delivery on all orders over $300 Australia-wide. For orders under $300, a flat shipping rate applies and is calculated at checkout based on order weight and destination. Standard delivery timeframes from the Braeside, Victoria dispatch centre: VIC / NSW / ACT: 1 to 3 business days QLD / SA / TAS: 2 to 4 business days WA / NT / Remote areas: 4 to 8 business days In-stock items are dispatched same or next business day. A tracking number is provided by email once the order leaves the warehouse. For large commercial orders, contact the team on 1800 617 341 to discuss lead times.     
